ChangeLog for Development Version

09-11-2026 Raja Zahidi
- UI & Feature: Overhauled, enlarged, and fixed Guitar Board & Tab:
  * Dramatically enlarged window from 600x150 to 1040x280 (min 740x200) with
    responsive wxBoxSizer and dynamic fret/string resizing.
  * Added authentic TAB headstock header with string tuning names (e B G D A E
    for 6-string guitar, G D A E for 4-string bass).
  * Added fret numbers (0 to 24) along bottom and pearl position inlay dots
    at standard frets (3, 5, 7, 9, 12 double-dot, 15, 17, 19, 21).
  * Fixed open string (fret 0) rendering and coordinate calculation bugs which
    previously filtered out open string notes.
  * Added realistic string thickness gauges and modern note badge markers.
  * Added real-time sound synthesis on click & drag across fretboard.
  * Fixed Guitar Settings dialog to properly load, configure (fret count 17-24,
    bass/guitar, octaves, chord mode), and apply settings immediately.
  * Added "Guitar Board & Tab..." entry to TrackFrame Tools menu (Ctrl+G).
- Fix: Removed duplicate MIDI Effects, Procedural SFX & Audio DSP items from
  Tools menu. Effects items now appear exclusively under the Effects menu.
- Fix & Stability: Fretboard dimension safeguards and mouse capture handling:
  * Protected against potential division-by-zero in fretboard dimension calculations
    when window is resized down.
  * Added EVT_MOUSE_CAPTURE_LOST handling and HasCapture() validation to prevent
    Windows assertions during mouse click-and-drag.
  * Ensured StopNote() unconditionally resets playing note state and is invoked on window destruction.
  * Replaced float abs() with std::fabs() in AudioEffects biquad filter.
- Fix & Portability: Automatic discovery and setup of jazz.cfg and definition files:
  * Resolved "Please Indicate the Location of jazz.cfg" dialog on fresh installs
    and portable runs by implementing multi-candidate directory searching across
    exeDir/conf, dataDir/conf, userConfigDir, and working directory.
  * Enhanced InsureConfigurationFileExistence() to automatically copy default conf
    and .jzi synthesizer files from candidate paths to UserConfigDir.
  * Enhanced FindFile() to seamlessly locate included .jzi files in conf/ subdirectories.
  * Packaged jazz.cfg into both package root and conf/ in Windows release ZIP.
- Credit: Added "Developer" label to Raja Zahidi entry in About dialog.
- Credit: Added Raja Zahidi name, copyright headers across all new source files,
  and updated build number to 15 in JazzPlusPlusVersion.h.

09-10-2026 Raja Zahidi
- Fix: Dialog windows (MIDI Effects Suite, Procedural SFX & Drum Synthesizer,
  Audio Effects DSP) were collapsing to a very small size on open. Root cause
  was use of wxScrolledWindow for tab pages combined with SetSizeHints() which
  computed near-zero minimum sizes. Fixed by reverting tab pages to wxPanel and
  replacing SetSizeHints() with Fit() + explicit minimum size clamping.

09-09-2026 Raja Zahidi
- Fix: Dialog layout and sizing for MIDI Effects and Sound Generator dialogs.
  Increased default sizes, added minimum size constraints and scroll support.
- Fix: Crash when clicking on track/channel selector in PianoFrame. Fixed null
  pointer dereference and channel adjustment logic.
- Add: MIDI Effects Suite (Arpeggiator, Humanizer, Harmonizer, MIDI Echo)
  - src/MidiEffects.h, src/MidiEffects.cpp
  - src/Dialogs/MidiEffectsDialog.h, src/Dialogs/MidiEffectsDialog.cpp
  - Menu entries added to TrackFrame and PianoFrame under Tools & Effects menus
- Add: Procedural Sound FX & 808 Analog Drum Synthesizer
  - src/SoundGenerator.h, src/SoundGenerator.cpp
  - src/Dialogs/SoundGeneratorDialog.h, src/Dialogs/SoundGeneratorDialog.cpp
  - Retro Game SFX (8 presets), Analog Synth Drums (6 voices)
  - WAV export and track insertion support
- Add: Audio DSP Engine
  - src/AudioEffects.h, src/AudioEffects.cpp
  - src/Dialogs/AudioEffectsDialog.h, src/Dialogs/AudioEffectsDialog.cpp
  - 3-Band Parametric EQ, Freeverb Algorithmic Reverb, Stereo Delay & Echo,
    Stereo Chorus/Flanger, Master Limiter & Overdrive/Distortion
  - Play preview and apply-to-sample-slot support
- Add: Comprehensive automated unit test suite (185 tests) covering all new
  MIDI effects, sound generator, and audio DSP classes via CTest.

09-08-2026 Raja Zahidi
- Fix: Core stability and crash when clicking on PRG / track channel selector.
  Patched null pointer checks in TrackDialog and PianoFrame event handling.
- Fix: Modern audio subsystem — immediate ALSA PCM flushing, auto-loading of
  samples, and dynamic MIDI device selection.
- Fix: Audio null pointer crash in EditAudioGlobalSettings, implemented modern
  JZAudioSettingsDialog for configuring audio devices and sample rates.
- Add: SoundFont switching utility and integrated high-quality SoundFont support.
- UI: Display note names on Piano Roll keyboard keys and note rectangles.
- UI: Fixed piano roll opening via double-click and menus, synchronized scrolling.
- Build & Docs: Generated missing HTML help files to fix 'Cannot Find Help File
  jazz.hhp' startup popup. Fixed CI build on Ubuntu 22.04 with GCC 11 and
  wxWidgets 3.0 compatibility.

03-23-04
-Added the XRC library and make a Makefile.am for it.
-Removed the configure and Makefile.in entries from the CVS.  They keep
 changing, and it's annoying to keep them current in the CVS.

03-21-04 Patrick Earl
-I forget to make log entries, so this is one huge entry to describe the
 changes I've made over time.  I'm no doubt missing many smaller changes.
-Separated most of tPianoWin from tEventWin.  There are still minor pieces that
 aren't finished, but at least tEventWin is no longer tPianoWin's superclass.
-Fixed a number of issues with coordinate translation in the piano window.
-Fixed some of the redraw stuff and the tMouseCounter update thing.
-Created a new dialog system based on XRC.  The code for that is in resdlg.c
 and resdlg.h.
-Removed the AUDIO #ifdef.  I didn't see much of a reason to complicate the
 code and leave the ability to remove the audio component.  If the audio
 portion of Jazz is broken, it should be either fixed or removed.  If it's
 working, I see no reason to not make it available for use all the time.
 Adding the additional compile time switch just adds complexity to the code.
 If no audio device is available, that condition can be detected and dealt
 with at run-time.
-Fixed the bitmap "make" script.  Also fixed a number of the bitmaps to
 properly handle transparency.
-Integrated patch to support midi devices other than 0.
-Removed all the misused #pragma hdrstop directives.
-Created new XRC Window Settings dialog for the piano and track windows.
-Removed the wxwin2port.h file and properly dealt with any issues that caused.

03-15-04 Patrick Earl
-Rewrote toolbar.cpp and toolbar.h
-Updated all references to toolbar system and removed the crazy tb_ stuff.
-Rewrote the note colourization in the piano window.  Now allocates on stack.


